{%- comment -%}
  CAVIERA — THREE WORLDS — complete four-part scroll experience

  STATUS: all four worlds (00 Threshold, 01 The Constant, 02 The Editions, 03 Private Commissions)
  are built with final approved imagery, copy, and motion and wired into the homepage.

  This section owns and loads its OWN stylesheet and script directly (see the two tags at the
  bottom) rather than relying on layout/theme.liquid's global asset list — the same
  self-contained pattern already used elsewhere in this theme (e.g. sections/caviera-hero.liquid's
  own script tag).

  FOUR WORLDS, each a real element the isolated JS can independently address via its own
  data-world value: "threshold", "constant", "editions", "commissions". Deliberately NOT four
  ordinary stacked Shopify sections — this is one section containing four full-viewport world
  wrappers, so world-to-world transitions can be handled by one shared, pinned scroll architecture
  without restructuring the page into separate sections.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'caviera-three-worlds.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  Threshold uses the approved static master image and the shared production scroll engine.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="caviera-three-worlds"
  data-caviera-three-worlds
  data-c3w-threshold-mode="video-scrub"
  data-threshold-video-src="{{ 'caviera-three-worlds-threshold-motion-2026.mp4' | asset_url }}"
>

  {%- comment -%} ================= 00 — THE THRESHOLD ================= {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    STAGE/STICKY-INNER (Phase 2b) — added because the scroll-driven reveal sequence below needs
    real scroll DISTANCE to scrub across; the plain .c3w-world base rule Threshold otherwise shares
    with every other world is exactly one viewport tall, which made entryExitProgress() (assets/
    caviera-three-worlds.js) degenerate to a binary 0-or-1 snap instead of a continuous 0–1 value —
    confirmed by direct measurement before this fix (min-height: 100vh means rect.height - vh = 0).
    This is the SAME "in-flow tall ancestor + sticky pinned inner" pattern already established
    elsewhere in this theme for exactly this reason — see sections/caviera-editorial-media.liquid's
    own .caviera-editorial__stage/-inner for its scroll_progression feature. data-world="threshold"
    stays on the OUTER (tall) element, since that's what the JS actually measures; the sticky inner
    is purely visual and carries no data attributes of its own.
    230vh keeps Threshold the shortest world while adding a modest amount of entrance breathing
    room; the existing progress mapping prevents an overlong text-free corridor beat.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section
    class="c3w-world c3w-world--threshold"
    data-world="threshold"
    data-world-index="0"
    aria-label="The Threshold"
  >
    <div class="c3w-threshold__stage">
      {%- comment -%}
        THRESHOLD MEDIA — FINAL, per Phase 2c: the approved master still (assets/caviera-three-
        worlds-threshold-2026.png, 1672x941 native, 16:9) remains the permanent static Threshold
        environment and the video prototype's loading/failure fallback. Untouched by any CSS
        transform, shown via
        plain object-fit: cover so its own centred corridor axis stays centred regardless of
        viewport aspect ratio. The image itself never moves/animates beyond the approved one-time
        entry settle (scale 1.015→1, see --threshold-environment-scale) — the "living" feeling below
        comes entirely from the two light layers composited on top of it, never from the image.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-threshold__media" data-threshold-media>
        <img
          class="c3w-threshold__media-el"
          src="{{ 'caviera-three-worlds-threshold-2026.png' | asset_url }}"
          width="1672" height="941"
          alt=""
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        >
        {%- comment -%}
          Living-light layers (Phase 2c) — two lightweight, opacity-only radial gradients, both
          entirely CSS (assets/caviera-three-worlds.css), driven by --threshold-light-primary-
          opacity / --threshold-light-secondary-opacity (assets/caviera-three-worlds.js). Sit above
          the image, below the typography (.c3w-world__inner's z-index: 1 still wins); pointer-
          events: none so they can never intercept the ENTER THE HOUSE click. Contained entirely
          inside .c3w-threshold__media — cannot affect Constant/Editions/Commissions.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="c3w-threshold__light" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="c3w-threshold__light-secondary" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="c3w-threshold-video" aria-hidden="true">
        <video
          class="c3w-threshold-video__el"
          data-threshold-video
          muted
          playsinline
          preload="auto"
          poster="{{ 'caviera-three-worlds-threshold-2026.png' | asset_url }}"
        ></video>
      </div>

      <div class="c3w-world__inner c3w-threshold__inner">
        <div class="c3w-threshold__mark">
          {%- comment -%}
            Official CAVIERA wordmark asset — never retyped. mode: 'dark' renders the Bone-coloured
            version, correct against this world's Obsidian field (same convention as the header's
            own transparent-over-dark-hero case).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- render 'caviera-wordmark', mode: 'dark', width: 220, loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high' -%}
        </div>
        <p class="c3w-threshold__eyebrow">CAVIERA JEWELS</p>
        {%- comment -%}
          Two lines, each individually masked (overflow: hidden on the outer span, the inner span
          itself carrying the actual translateY reveal) rather than a generic fade-up — per brief,
          "preferred treatment: masked/clipped vertical reveal". Live HTML text throughout, nothing
          baked into the image.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <h1 class="c3w-threshold__heading">
          <span class="c3w-threshold__heading-line"><span>THE HOUSE EXISTS</span></span>
          <span class="c3w-threshold__heading-line"><span>IN THREE FORMS.</span></span>
        </h1>
        <button type="button" class="c3w-threshold__cta" data-world-enter aria-label="Enter the House — scroll to The Constant">
          <span>ENTER THE HOUSE</span>
        </button>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Foreground layer — empty hook only (Step 3's conceptual media/environment/content/foreground
        stack). No visual effect in Phase 1 (no vignette, grain, or particles exist yet); a later
        phase can add real content here without touching this world's markup structure again.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-world__foreground" data-layer="foreground" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- render 'caviera-three-worlds-transition', from: 'threshold', to: 'constant' -%}

  {%- comment -%} ================= 01 — THE CONSTANT ================= {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    STAGE/STICKY-INNER (Phase 3a) — same "in-flow tall ancestor + sticky pinned inner" pattern as
    the Threshold (see that section's own comment above for the measured bug this avoids: a plain
    one-viewport-tall world can only ever produce a binary 0-or-1 entryExitProgress, never a
    continuous 0–1 value to scrub a reveal sequence across). The 440vh outer canvas gives the three
    approved detail photographs true observation holds and preserves a composed Permanence state.
    data-world="constant" stays on the OUTER (tall)
    element — exactly what entryExitProgress() and the orientation indicator's own geometry read.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section
    class="c3w-world c3w-world--constant"
    data-world="constant"
    data-world-index="1"
    aria-label="01 — The Constant"
  >
    <div class="c3w-constant__stage">
      {%- comment -%}
        MASTER CONSTANT ENVIRONMENT (Phase 3b, FINAL) — approved asset, untouched/unfiltered.
        object-position: center center — verified visually at 1366/1440/1600/1920 that this keeps
        the central Warm Bone archive monolith, the paired vertical ribs and the distant Cinnabar
        recess all in frame (the source is 1672x941, 16:9, close enough to every required viewport
        aspect that cropping is minor and symmetric, exactly like the Threshold's own still).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-constant__media" data-constant-media>
        <img
          class="c3w-constant__media-el"
          src="{{ 'caviera-three-worlds-constant-2026.png' | asset_url }}"
          width="1672" height="941"
          alt=""
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        >
      </div>
      {%- comment -%}
        Living light (Phase 3b) — positioned over the master image's own existing warm-lit stone
        wall behind the monolith (~60% across, ~45% down), not a new light source. Two additional
        code-specific emphasis layers sit alongside it: MATERIAL brightens the stone/brass wall
        further, RITUAL brightens the monolith itself — both driven by that code's own "distance
        from its window's midpoint" (assets/caviera-three-worlds.js), so they rise and recede as a
        continuous part of the same scroll, never a hard toggle.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-constant__environment" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="c3w-constant__material-emphasis" data-constant-code="material" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="c3w-constant__ritual-emphasis" data-constant-code="ritual" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      {%- comment -%}
        CODE 01 — HOUSE SEAL: the official mark, positioned over the small circular brass inset
        already visible on the monolith's own surface in the master image (~50% across, ~61% down —
        located by inspection, not guessed) — authentication built into the architecture itself,
        never a redrawn/generated mark. Sized modestly (56px) per brief ("should feel like
        authentication, not decoration").
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-constant__seal-mark" data-constant-code="seal" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- render 'caviera-house-seal', mode: 'dark', width: 56 -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        CODE 02 — ORYX: the official Living Oryx mark (never a new drawing), placed beside the
        master image's own paired tall vertical ribs (~63% across) so the reveal reads as
        recognition — "this is why the architecture has this geometry" — rather than a mascot
        dropped into the room. Modest scale (110px).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-constant__oryx-mark" data-constant-code="oryx" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- render 'caviera-oryx', variant: 'static', mode: 'dark', width: 110 -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        CODE 03 — PROVENANCE: the approved detail image as a large controlled vertical frame
        (52–68vh tall, native 4:5 ratio preserved via aspect-ratio, not stretched), offset toward
        the stage's own right-of-centre — deliberately not a centred ecommerce card. The image's own
        blank recessed oval sits at approximately 71%/43% of its own frame (located by inspection);
        rather than stretching the tall, narrow official House Seal artwork to fill that wide,
        shallow oval (which would distort it — the two shapes don't match), a small, modestly-sized
        seal is centred INSIDE the recess at its native proportions via object-fit: contain, exactly
        the brief's own sanctioned approach when a full-bleed fill isn't accurate. Centre-point
        alignment only (not edge-to-edge fitting) stays precise across every viewport width because
        the frame's own aspect-ratio is fixed (never independently cropped per axis like a cover
        image would be) — verified visually after implementation, not assumed.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-constant__provenance" data-constant-code="provenance" data-detail="provenance" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="c3w-constant__provenance-frame">
          <img
            class="c3w-constant__provenance-el"
            src="{{ 'caviera-three-worlds-constant-provenance-2026.png' | asset_url }}"
            width="1122" height="1402"
            alt=""
            loading="lazy"
          >
          <div class="c3w-constant__provenance-seal">
            {%- render 'caviera-house-seal', mode: 'dark', width: 34 -%}
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="c3w-constant__provenance-caption">Recorded by the House.</p>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        WebGL Provenance authentication mark — the same official snippet and native proportions as
        the static detail above, independently positioned because the static frame is suppressed
        only after Constant WebGL has proved its own first frame. Never a redraw or canvas copy.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-constant__webgl-provenance-seal" data-constant-code="provenance" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- render 'caviera-house-seal', mode: 'dark', width: 34 -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        CODE 04 — MATERIAL (Phase 3c, FINAL — approved detail asset, untouched/unfiltered). Shares
        the same .c3w-constant__detail architecture as Ritual below (per brief, "extend cleanly,
        avoid three separate fragile systems") — Provenance's own already-locked markup/classes
        above are deliberately left untouched rather than merged into this, so nothing about its
        approved implementation can regress. Positioned left-of-centre, bottom-anchored — clear of
        the text column (which ends well before this frame's own left edge at every required
        width) and deliberately NOT the same slot Provenance occupies, per brief ("a different
        spatial position... does not feel like the same image slot changing content").
        CONSTANT_MATERIAL_DETAIL_SLOT is now filled — this comment name is kept only so a future
        pass searching for it still finds this exact spot.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-constant__detail" data-constant-code="material" data-detail="material" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="c3w-constant__detail-frame">
          <img
            class="c3w-constant__detail-el"
            src="{{ 'caviera-three-worlds-constant-material-2026.png' | asset_url }}"
            width="1122" height="1402"
            alt=""
            loading="lazy"
          >
        </div>
        <p class="c3w-constant__detail-caption">Stone. Metal. Form.</p>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        CODE 05 — RITUAL (Phase 3c, FINAL — approved detail asset, untouched/unfiltered). Same
        shared .c3w-constant__detail architecture as Material above. Right-of-centre like
        Provenance (same architectural "edge" of the room) but bottom-anchored rather than
        vertically centred, so the two never read as the same picture-frame slot cycling content —
        per brief, "slightly lower or opposite side... choose based on actual visual balance".
        CONSTANT_RITUAL_DETAIL_SLOT is now filled — comment name kept for the same reason as above.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-constant__detail" data-constant-code="ritual" data-detail="ritual" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="c3w-constant__detail-frame">
          <img
            class="c3w-constant__detail-el"
            src="{{ 'caviera-three-worlds-constant-ritual-2026.png' | asset_url }}"
            width="1122" height="1402"
            alt=""
            loading="lazy"
          >
        </div>
        <p class="c3w-constant__detail-caption">Every object enters the House the same way.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="c3w-world__inner c3w-constant__content">
        {%- comment -%}
          Intro group (index/title/statement/supporting) — positioned upper-left via
          .c3w-constant__content's own CSS (not centred like the Threshold) specifically to leave
          the central monolith and the distant Cinnabar recess both clearly visible below/right of
          the type. Recedes to a quieter, still-legible state once the code narrative begins (see
          --c3w-constant-intro-opacity/-scale) — per brief, "does not need to remain giant
          throughout... the world identity must remain understandable."
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="c3w-constant__intro">
          <span class="c3w-constant__index">01</span>
          <h2 class="c3w-constant__title">
            <span class="c3w-constant__title-line"><span>THE CONSTANT</span></span>
          </h2>
          <p class="c3w-constant__statement">WHAT REMAINS.</p>
          <p class="c3w-constant__supporting">The permanent codes of the House.</p>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          Six permanent-code narrative markers (Phase 3b, FINAL treatment) — NOT a menu of six
          always-visible labels. Each code now carries TWO elements sharing the same data-constant-
          code hook (assets/caviera-three-worlds.js already sets data-code-state on every matching
          element, so no JS change was needed for this): a small persistent index tick (part of a
          quiet six-number ladder — the ONLY thing always visible, dimmed per the existing active/
          past/future opacities) and a full label+line pair that only reads clearly while its own
          code is active (grid-stacked in the same cell as every other code's copy, so the visitor
          never sees more than one at a time and nothing ever jumps in height as they scroll).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="c3w-constant__code-ladder" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="c3w-constant__code-tick" data-constant-code="seal">01</span>
          <span class="c3w-constant__code-tick" data-constant-code="oryx">02</span>
          <span class="c3w-constant__code-tick" data-constant-code="provenance">03</span>
          <span class="c3w-constant__code-tick" data-constant-code="material">04</span>
          <span class="c3w-constant__code-tick" data-constant-code="ritual">05</span>
          <span class="c3w-constant__code-tick" data-constant-code="permanence">06</span>
        </div>
        <div class="c3w-constant__code-copy-stack" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="c3w-constant__code-copy" data-constant-code="seal">
            <p class="c3w-constant__code-label">House Seal</p>
            <p class="c3w-constant__code-line">The mark of the House.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="c3w-constant__code-copy" data-constant-code="oryx">
            <p class="c3w-constant__code-label">Oryx</p>
            <p class="c3w-constant__code-line">The geometry that guides the House.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="c3w-constant__code-copy" data-constant-code="provenance">
            <p class="c3w-constant__code-label">Provenance</p>
            <p class="c3w-constant__code-line">Recorded by the House.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="c3w-constant__code-copy" data-constant-code="material">
            <p class="c3w-constant__code-label">Material</p>
            <p class="c3w-constant__code-line">Stone. Metal. Form.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="c3w-constant__code-copy" data-constant-code="ritual">
            <p class="c3w-constant__code-label">Ritual</p>
            <p class="c3w-constant__code-line">Every object enters the House the same way.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="c3w-constant__code-copy" data-constant-code="permanence">
            <p class="c3w-constant__code-label">Permanence</p>
            <p class="c3w-constant__code-line">What is recorded, remains.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="c3w-world__foreground" data-layer="foreground" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- render 'caviera-three-worlds-transition', from: 'constant', to: 'editions' -%}

  {%- comment -%} ================= 02 — THE EDITIONS ================= {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    STAGE/STICKY-INNER (Phase 4) — same proven "tall in-flow ancestor + sticky pinned inner"
    architecture as Threshold/Constant, per brief's own instruction to reuse it rather than invent a
    new one. The 360vh outer canvas provides full holds for Light Study and Reveal Stage, plus a
    final composed First Light state. data-world="editions"
    stays on the OUTER (tall) element — what entryExitProgress() and the orientation indicator's own
    geometry both read.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section
    class="c3w-world c3w-world--editions"
    data-world="editions"
    data-world-index="2"
    aria-label="02 — The Editions"
  >
    <div class="c3w-editions__stage">
      {%- comment -%}
        MASTER ENVIRONMENT (Phase 4, FINAL — approved asset, untouched/unfiltered).
        assets/caviera-three-worlds-editions-first-light-2026.png, 1672x941 native (16:9, same
        proportions as the Threshold's and Constant's own master stills). object-position: center
        centre — verified visually at 1366/1440/1600/1920 that the diagonal First Light beam, the
        Warm Bone plane, the Cinnabar architecture, the dark platform and the reflective floor all
        stay in frame; the source's near-16:9 aspect keeps cropping minor and symmetric at every
        required width, exactly like the other two worlds' own stills.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-editions__media" data-editions-media>
        <img
          class="c3w-editions__media-el"
          src="{{ 'caviera-three-worlds-editions-first-light-2026.png' | asset_url }}"
          width="1672" height="941"
          alt=""
          loading="lazy"
        >
      </div>
      {%- comment -%}
        First Light emphasis (Phase 4) — the approved still ALREADY contains the diagonal beam; this
        is a single restrained CSS gradient at roughly the same angle, subtly rising then receding
        with scroll (assets/caviera-three-worlds.js), never a second obvious beam, never neon, never
        an automatic keyframe loop.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-editions__first-light" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      {%- comment -%}
        Exit scrim (Phase 4) — per brief, "scene darkens subtly... Cinnabar becomes quieter" as
        Editions prepares to release into Private Commissions. Simply dropping the media's own
        opacity was tried first and rejected: this world's own background is Cinnabar (unchanged
        from Phase 1), so fading the image without this scrim exposed MORE red underneath it, the
        opposite of "quieter" — confirmed via screenshot, not assumed. A plain Obsidian scrim rising
        in opacity only during the final 0.90–1.00 window mutes everything beneath it uniformly.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-editions__exit-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="c3w-world__inner c3w-editions__content">
        {%- comment -%}
          World identity (02 / THE EDITIONS / WHAT CHANGES.) then the current Edition's own identity
          (EDITION I / THE FIRST LIGHT) — live HTML throughout, integrated into the architecture via
          .c3w-editions__content's own upper-left position (see CSS), never a centred poster. "THE
          EDITIONS" reuses the same masked-vertical-line TECHNIQUE as Threshold/Constant's own
          headings (an independent progress window, not copied timing); the Edition identity below
          it is deliberately smaller/precise ("campaign-style"), not a second giant headline.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="c3w-editions__index">02</span>
        <h2 class="c3w-editions__title">
          <span class="c3w-editions__title-line"><span>THE EDITIONS</span></span>
        </h2>
        <p class="c3w-editions__statement">WHAT CHANGES.</p>
        <div class="c3w-editions__edition">
          <p class="c3w-editions__edition-number">Edition I</p>
          <p class="c3w-editions__edition-name">The First Light</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        DETAIL 01 — LIGHT STUDY (Phase 4, FINAL). Shares the same shared-architecture PRINCIPLE as
        Constant's own .c3w-constant__detail (per brief, reuse the proven pattern) but is its own
        separate class, .c3w-editions__detail, so nothing about the already-locked Constant
        implementation is touched. Positioned right-of-centre, TOP-anchored — deliberately not the
        same spot used by any of Constant's three details (right/centre, left/bottom, right/bottom),
        and not the same spot Reveal Stage below uses either.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-editions__detail" data-editions-detail="light-study" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="c3w-editions__detail-frame">
          <img
            class="c3w-editions__detail-el"
            src="{{ 'caviera-three-worlds-editions-light-study-2026.png' | asset_url }}"
            width="1122" height="1402"
            alt=""
            loading="lazy"
          >
        </div>
        <p class="c3w-editions__detail-label">The First Light</p>
        <p class="c3w-editions__detail-caption">Light becomes form.</p>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        DETAIL 02 — REVEAL STAGE (Phase 4, FINAL). The empty architectural platform is intentional —
        per brief, absolutely no jewellery/product imagery yet. Left-of-centre, bottom-anchored — a
        different position from Light Study above, and larger (see CSS) so it reads as more dominant.
        Edition I naming remains locked to the approved title "The First Light".
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="c3w-editions__detail c3w-editions__detail--reveal-stage" data-editions-detail="reveal-stage" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="c3w-editions__detail-frame">
          <img
            class="c3w-editions__detail-el"
            src="{{ 'caviera-three-worlds-editions-reveal-stage-2026.png' | asset_url }}"
            width="1122" height="1402"
            alt=""
            loading="lazy"
          >
        </div>
        <p class="c3w-editions__detail-label">The First Light</p>
      </div>

      <div class="c3w-world__foreground" data-layer="foreground" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- render 'caviera-three-worlds-transition', from: 'editions', to: 'commissions' -%}

  {%- comment -%} ================= 03 — PRIVATE COMMISSIONS ================= {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    STAGE/STICKY-INNER (Phase 5) — same proven architecture as Threshold/Constant/Editions. The
    500vh outer canvas gives all five photographs observation time and preserves the final CTA hold.
    data-world="commissions"
    stays on the OUTER (tall) element, unchanged from Phase 1.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section
    class="c3w-world c3w-world--commissions"
    data-world="commissions"
    data-world-index="3"
    aria-label="03 — Private Commissions"
  >
    <div class="c3w-private__stage">
      {%- comment -%}
        MASTER ENVIRONMENT (Phase 5, FINAL — approved source asset untouched; desktop exposure is
        controlled non-destructively in CSS).
        assets/caviera-three-worlds-private-commissions-2026.png, 1672x941 native (16:9, same
